LC 3 — Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters
Pattern:Sliding Window + Hashing

Logic:
Keep a window with no duplicate characters.
j expands the window.
If duplicate appears, move i forward.
Keep the maximum length.

Algorithm:
i = 0
j = 0

While j < string length:
    if s[j] already exists:
        move i forward
    add s[j]
    update maximum length
    j++

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    int lengthOfLongestSubstring(string s) {
        unordered_set<char> st;
        int i = 0, ans = 0;

        for (int j = 0; j < s.size(); j++) {
            while (st.count(s[j])) {
                st.erase(s[i]);
                i++;
            }

            st.insert(s[j]);
            ans = max(ans, j - i + 1);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};

EX:
s = "abcabcbb"

"abc" → 3 unique ✅

next 'a' → duplicate ❌
remove old 'a'
"bca" → 3 unique ✅

next 'b' → duplicate ❌
remove old 'b'
"cab" → 3 unique ✅

Answer = 3 ✅


